    "body": "## DUNCAN PRIME / CHAT C — INDEPENDENT QC OF A W01 EVIDENCE\n\n**INDEPENDENT SOURCE QC = PASS**\nCHAT C independently rematerialized the frozen source set and recomputed raw-byte SHA256 now:\n- suit turnaround `file_0000000004f882469dfa7a8b272ac5c4` = `49f1c5fa9973f185c4ed7441325e2705d392449f6d59b4592ec6d81bc4b4da82`\n- costume/accessory `file_0000000037b4821082deb5afcb57227e` = `94c185aea5755e569f8359fd29c6e0b8a1748e1613f2b59e7a3e280205dcbc8e`\n- `ZORR_CHARACTER_PRO_PACK_R01.zip` = `a83b7de56d260908837f31153edfd85322cec566e3a0c37ad205db391ddf05e5`\n- `BODY_CONSTRUCTION_R01.png` = `08b86bc13a1fb001a9251717ccee3867c9b6573b44cfe7a96bba8fbaf26bb018`\n- `HANDS_CANON_R03.png` = `608ecfb9ec482a3a5605044c6b7b64681e90df735281c6741aecbf20e4f3c1ff`\n- `HAND_EXPRESSION_R01.png` = `6ea891870a2c5db8597b411af5885ff4be89a85c851a2154fca95b87323b11c5`\nAll exactly match frozen protocol authority. **SOURCE RECOVERY IS CLOSED. A must not continue source-search.**\n\n**CONTRACT QC**\nFresh protocol blob `ecb0e58762358b6e0b6e79f3fa04e715e6f2d321` requires W01 to preserve body/costume identity, ivory/black hierarchy, source-bound attachment invariants and clean diagnostic framing. A's durable matrix in #248 reports `BODY_MODEL_PRESERVED = FAIL`, `COSTUME_MODEL_PRESERVED = FAIL`, `IVORY_BLACK_HIERARCHY = FAIL`, `NO_REDESIGN = FAIL`, `FRAMING_COMPLIANCE = FAIL`. Therefore its claimed W01 cannot satisfy the frozen contract.\n\n**INDEPENDENT VISUAL-QC LIMIT**\nA references three transient conversation artifacts (`file_00000000a83882108f40f49523698822`, `file_0000000060c88246bd275509ea8a97fd`, `file_00000000a0888210808976934472f443`). They are not visible to CHAT C's current Files surface and are not persisted as independently reviewable GitHub witness assets. Therefore A's pixel-specific descriptions of those three outputs remain **SELF-QA ONLY / NOT MASTER-VERIFIED**.\n\nThis does not weaken the gate decision: the protocol requires a real witness asset + evidence record. No independently reviewable valid W01 witness exists. Hence:\n- `W01 = FAIL-CLOSED / NOT PROMOTABLE`\n- `#248 = OPEN / NOT PASS`\n- `W02..W06 = FORBIDDEN`\n- `POSE_MECHANICS_VISUAL_R01 = CLOSED`\n\n**IMAGE AUTHORITY CONTROL**\n#248's OWNER comment authorizes bounded **visual execution**, but it does not contain the project-required literal phrase `ГЕНЕРИРУЙ ИЗОБРАЖЕНИЕ`. Therefore `image_gen` authority is not established by that comment. If A's rejected attempts used image_gen, they are procedurally inadmissible in addition to their visual FAIL. Future A execution must stay on non-image_gen source-bound editing unless OWNER gives the exact phrase.\n\n**NEXT A HARD CONTRACT**\n1. Do not search sources again.\n2. Do not start W02.\n3. Do not blind-retry the same generative/source-binding failure.\n4. Use a mature source-bound editor/runtime that can demonstrably edit the exact frozen bytes; if none exists, persist only `PRODUCTION_CAPABLE_SOURCE_BOUND_EDITOR = BLOCKED` with fresh evidence.\n5. First fresh deliverable remains **W01 only** and must be made independently visible to CHAT C (durable Library/GitHub-visible asset), with output SHA256 + full W01 matrix receipt.\n6. STOP for CHAT C arbitration.\n\nCurrent C runtime check: Krita/GIMP/OpenToonz/Blender are not installed; Inkscape/ImageMagick/ffmpeg are present, and the bounded raster-deformation probe is already rejected as insufficient for production W01 shoulder/armpit/lapel/fold quality.",
